# Rules router

Rules are grouped in pack folders under `.cursor/rules/`. Only installed packs exist in this project. Most rules attach by file glob; the rest are agent-requested, so read any rule whose description matches the task before editing.

| Pack | Applies to |
|------|------------|
| `core/` | Any project: docs sync, deploy safety |
| `laravel/` | Laravel backend (`app/`, `bootstrap/`, `config/`, `database/`, `routes/`) |
| `qwik/` | Qwik City frontend (`src/routes`, `src/lib`, `vite.config.ts`) |
| `nuxt/` | Nuxt frontend (`pages/`, `components/`, `composables/`, `server/`) |
| `admin/` | Admin dashboard routes and components |
| `public-site/` | Public pages: SEO, head tags, assets, contact privacy |
| `cms-builder/` | Visual page/theme builder and addon host (Credocode-based projects) |
| `wordpress/` | WordPress themes and plugins |
| `react-native/` | React Native / Expo apps (`app/`, `src/`, `app.json`, `plugins/`) |

Skills (load on demand from `.cursor/skills/`): `new-project`, `deploy`, `laravel-hardening`, `qwik-ssr-debug`, `builder-json-translation`, `expo-upgrade`.

## Git

Commit, push, or deploy only when the user asks.

## Project rules

Pack folders come from the shared rules library; change shared rules there, not in this copy. Project-only rules go in `.cursor/rules/project/`: frontmatter on line 1, `alwaysApply: false`, `**/`-prefixed comma-separated globs, and nothing the global User Rule already says.
